@ 32.1.3 - Proto-Chatino to Yaitepec Chatino
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Upson, B.W., and Robert E. Longacre (1965), “Proto-Chatino Phonology”. International Journal of American Linguistics 31(4):312 – 322 Some consonant disharmony involving reflexes of *k, *kʷ
	tʲ > tj
	k > t͡ʃ / _Ekʷ
	kʲ > k / _{a,ã}
	kʲ > kj / else
	kʷ > w / _e:[+long]j
	kʷ > w / _ek
	kʷ > ʍ / ku_ (medial)
	kʷ > kw / else
	t͡s > t͡ʃ / #_{a,õ}ʔ
	t͡s > t͡ʃ / V:[+high]_
	t͡s > ʃ / #_ẽ
	c > t͡s
	t͡ʃ > t͡s / a_
	s > ʃ / V_V
	s > ʃ / if /l/ is present in the same syllable
	s > t͡ʃ / #_a
	ʃ > s / _{ik,e,ı̃,ẽ}
	ʃ > t͡s / _i, in monosyllables
	lʲ > l / #_ in U:[-long -stress]
	lʲ > lj / else
	nʲ > j / _ã (with some exceptions?)
	nʲ > nj / else
	h > ʔ / _ã
	ç > hj
	hʷ > ʍ
	ẽ > ı̃ / {t,h}_#
	ẽ > ı̃ / _ʔ#
	ẽ > ı̃ / ʔ_# “in one case”